draphsor@deathstar.stanford.edu (Matt Rollefson) writes:

>30k? Hell, I've got > $100k right now with no real problems. Gold is
>really light, basically.

Eh, well, you mean "gold is VALUABLE."

I don't see any problem with the Gold unit of currency in NetHack.  A
"gold piece" could be a tiny wufffer-thin flake of gold, for all we
know.  

Copper pieces and silver pieces are, IMO, useless.  How much would Grayswndr
(or whatever the Silver Sword is called) be worth?  How about Bronze Plate?

Copper and Silver are really only useful in token currencies... which the
hack-slash world of NetHack wouldn't be likely to abide by:

	Progesterone offers you 1000 silver pieces for your mace -- more --
	Sell? Y
	10 gold pieces for that excellent potion -- more --
	Progesterone laughs "Silver?  Gold, only, cobber."
	You manage to make the hilt of Grayswndr with your 1000 solver pieces.

On this note, I like the idea of a weaponsmith, perhaps at the entrance to
the Gnomish mines - you order a big slasher on the way down, and pick it up
(and pay it off) on your way out.  Besides, a weaponsmith is exactly what
you'd EXPECT at the top of a mine.

